{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen","id":1198332,"title":"Yay or Nay? Demon: the Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-22T08:44:36-07:00","id":1198332,"title":"Yay or Nay? Demon: the Fallen","content":"So, while I have zero interest in Descent (I don't care for the God Machine idea, and even less so for a game that revolves around it), I have been curious about Fallen for some time. Unfortunately, I seem to be getting mixed reviews about its themes and mechanics. Some people think it's good and are hoping for a D20 release, while others weren't too pleased with it, judging by how we don't even have a forum dedicated to it.<br /> <br /> Some have said that players weren't happy about it adhering primarily to Abrahamic faiths, but that's something I'm not really worried about. Vampire kind of already did that by incorporating the biblical God into the vampire origin story.<br /> <br /> Others have said the game doesn't really allow for cross faction groups, which is also something I'm not too worried about. I mean, I have yet to see a game where people are playing Camarilla / Sabbat in the same coterie.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, what I am concerned with is that there is barely any coverage surrounding this game, both in youtube videos and wikis as well. They just sort of skim through the game without giving an in depth look about its premise or setting. This makes me hesitant about buying it, since I don't like the idea of paying for a game I know almost nothing about and finding out later that it's not right for me.<br /> <br /> So far, I'm leaning towards 'yes,' but that's mostly from my own hype about being able to play an actual friggin demon set loose upon the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:54:19-07:00","id":1198348,"title":"","content":"It has a good fluff, its mechanics need polish.<br /> <br /> It's the one game where you absolutely need the players handbook: It adds the concept of rituals and the idea of creating your own Apocalyptic Form (complete with wings that can actually fly instead of just &quot;glide&quot; like the ones in the Basic), which are two really big aditions.<br /> <br /> Many preffer to port the Sphere system from mage rather than use Lore system. But that's on you. Lore system it's like Disciplines, but a little more flexible. If you add rituals it's like a potent form of Thaumaturgy. Personally I wouldn't have used the Discipline/Thaumaturgy system for Demons. Something like Exalted Charm trees or Mage Pillars/Spheres would have worked much better to give that oomph of &quot;Lores of Creation&quot;, but that's me.<br /> <br /> It's fluff it's VERY good if you like the whole Milton &quot;it's better to rule in hell than to serve in heaven&quot; vive (and aren't married with Werewolf cosmology). Demon it's to the judeocristian WoD cosmology what Werewolf it's to the animist WoD cosmology - it goes above and beyond Vampire in that regards (and perhaps that's why people complains more about Demon than Vampire)<br /> <br /> In my opinion it does lack of &quot;things to do&quot; when you're a member of a demonic faction. To give an example, when you're Sabbat you have the Sabbat agenda, belief system, and social structure providing a solid foundation for the game, your character has a supernatural background to build on.<br /> Perhaps because Demon has so little material there isn't a very detailed agenda for each faction (for instance, how can you build the &quot;faith weapon&quot; for a Faustian Win?) and very little details about organizations or goalposts. Also, Demons lack the clear purpose Hunters - you aren't driven to do anything but to get one or two Faith farms, after that you can do what you want. It's almost a sandbox in that sense.<br /> <br /> The Earthbound book it's the most lovecraftian book of all WoD that I've ever read. So there's that.<br /> <br /> It would be great to have a D20 to encompass all these books, and polish some mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-22-2018, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:59:32-07:00","id":1198351,"title":"","content":"Demon is an interesting game. I had a lot of doubts about it when I first stumbled across it and I have never played a true (pure-)Demon game, but I am using it in my current game, even though we played around with the lore and stuff to make it fit a non-abrahamitic cosmos (basically we already established The One as the Weaver Incarna of Patriachy, so that's what created Elohim as it's servants and Lucifer is a really complex concept that isn't fully explained yet in the game).<br /> <br /> Overall, I have the feeling Demons are really much, much weaker overall than splats like Werewolfs, Mages and Vampires, even Changelings (especially C20). This is kind of funny, when you look at what they think to be.<br /> Mechanic wise, the rulebook is a mess! There's rules all over the place and nothing is where you would search for it. Also, without the Players Guide, Apocalypse Forms are very static and kind of just something that &quot;might&quot; come in handy for your character. However, Players Guide introduces systems to modify the forms to make them fit your characters.<br /> Lores are an interesting thing, they're linear magical paths and you start with four available. Also there's a &quot;Torment&quot; form of each. This is where Demon becomes something different than the other games. The more you lose yourself to your pain and anger, the more you lose control over your powers while you also get much stronger. Even your Apocalypse Form will get buffed with Torment Powers.<br /> The whole Torment-thing works like an opposite to Humanity in Vampire, where you lose your conscience and morality the more points you gather, really nothing new but a bit more flexible overall (then again, there's no paths so a flexible system makes sense).<br /> <br /> Since there are only a hand full of different houses (9 Houses), each with 3 Lores (and two common lores, I believe the Players Guide to be essential to really get this system going. Also, being creative and inventing some more &quot;lost&quot; Lores is a very cool thing. Were're working on a Lore of Shadows atm, inspired by the Obtenebration Discipline. In fact, a lot of Lores seem quite similar to certain Disciplines or especially to the elemental paths of Koldunism. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Earthbound are your common enemies, even though they are nothing special in the core book. Just really powerfull, high Torment Demons with a lot of Lore points and a lot of allies. The &quot;Earthbound&quot; rule book would fix that problem, with additional Lores designed after the triatic Wyrm but I don't have the book, so I can't say much about it. When I design godlike enemies, they don't have a fixed amount of stats and my players don't necessarily need to know that. That way they're epic no matter what.<br /> <br /> A minor drawback: Since Lores are cast by a combined Dice-Pool of Attribute + Ability and there are literally no Lore using Appearance, this Attribute might not even be rolled once the entire story. It's even more useless than in other game lines.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd go for a Yay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T10:07:42-07:00","id":1198353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earthbound are your common enemies, even though they are nothing special in the core book. Just really powerfull, high Torment Demons with a lot of Lore points and a lot of allies. The &quot;Earthbound&quot; rule book would fix that problem, with additional Lores designed after the triatic Wyrm but I don't have the book, so I can't say much about it. When I design godlike enemies, they don't have a fixed amount of stats and my players don't necessarily need to know that. That way they're epic no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>That book it's very good, and really upgrades Earthbounds up to the point of changing their vive. A lot. After you read that book, Demon transforms in &quot;Angels/Demons vs Cthulhu&quot; (when you use them as antagonists, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T12:55:19-07:00","id":1198384,"title":"","content":"One of the metaphors that is sort of underplayed in Demon: the Fallen is that the player characters are essentially escaped prisoners who are have to deal with integrating back into regular life (through the humans they've possessed/merged with), fighting the trauma they have from millennia of imprisonment and war, and resisting the urge to get sucked back into the schemes of both imprisoned Demon Lords and Earthbound demons and their cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:14:22-07:00","id":1198403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198348#post1198348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the one game where you absolutely need the players handbook: It adds the concept of rituals and the idea of creating your own Apocalyptic Form (complete with wings that can actually fly instead of just &quot;glide&quot; like the ones in the Basic), which are two really big aditions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume by Player's Handbook, you mean Player's Guide?<br /> <br /> If so, I'm going to add it to my Wishlist on DriveTHRU. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198384#post1198384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the metaphors that is sort of underplayed in Demon: the Fallen is that the player characters are essentially escaped prisoners who are have to deal with integrating back into regular life (through the humans they've possessed/merged with), fighting the trauma they have from millennia of imprisonment and war, and resisting the urge to get sucked back into the schemes of both imprisoned Demon Lords and Earthbound demons and their cults.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy shit, I didn't even consider that metaphor! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:21:38-07:00","id":1198479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198353#post1198353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That book it's very good, and really upgrades Earthbounds up to the point of changing their vive. A lot. After you read that book, Demon transforms in &quot;Angels/Demons vs Cthulhu&quot; (when you use them as antagonists, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, that's not quite accurate. The horror that surrounds the Lovecraft mythos isn't about the existence of alien demon-gods. It's about revealing humanity's insignificance in the grand scope of the universe and us being incapable of accepting that realization. We like to believe that all life is precious and every individual is special. But those who are worshiped as gods in Lovecraft's mythology were sporadically created through the chaotic dreams of Azathoth. And if the creation of the gods themselves was little more than an accident, then there is nothing special about life at all. Which is probably why Shub-Niggurath (a fertility goddess) looks like a roiling mass of random body parts, instead of a seductive or motherly figure.<br /> <br /> <br /> The monsters in Lovecraft don't actively want to destroy us. In fact, they barely even acknowledge that we exist. They just go about their business and if we happen to get fucked up along the way, then so be it. They're billions of years old, they've been around long enough to know that the death of one planet's inhabitant isn't going to affect the universe in the slightest.<br /> <br /> The monsters from Lovecraft's stories aren't so much threats to be challenged, as they are forces of nature beyond our control. Once you give the characters a way to defend themselves or defeat the enemy, then you've missed the point of his work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T05:33:43-07:00","id":1198617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198479#post1198479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that's not quite accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Lovecraft is influential in a number of different ways. The aesthetic of his creations is probably more so than the cosmic horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is probably why Shub-Niggurath (a fertility goddess) looks like a roiling mass of random body parts, instead of a seductive or motherly figure. </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft didn't describe Shub-Niggurath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once you give the characters a way to defend themselves or defeat the enemy, then you've missed the point of his work. </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to include Lovecraft on that list, seeing as it's not that uncommon for his characters to do so. Also, he did multiple different types of horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:46:01-07:00","id":1198651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198617#post1198617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Lovecraft is influential in a number of different ways. The aesthetic of his creations is probably more so than the cosmic horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lovecraft didn't describe Shub-Niggurath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're going to have to include Lovecraft on that list, seeing as it's not that uncommon for his characters to do so. Also, he did multiple different types of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - From what I understand, the aesthetic of his creations were derived from his own prejudices and general dislike for the world around him. The 'unknowable terrors' that permeates his work symbolizes his xenophobia towards other cultures and ethnic groups.<br /> <br /> 2 - Yeah, I know that a bunch of different people expanded his mythos. I'm not knowledgeable on who did what, though. Plus, his work is public domain! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3 - Sure, they can challenge the little minions. But as for taking on the big leagues, the only real option is to lull them to sleep and pray to whatever powers are listening that they stay that way. How exactly do you fight against a creature who is so alien to our minds that the very sight of them causes our eyes to explode from their sockets as we are plunged into screaming madness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:04:37-07:00","id":1198689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - From what I understand, the aesthetic of his creations were derived from his own prejudices and general dislike for the world around him. The 'unknowable terrors' that permeates his work symbolizes his xenophobia towards other cultures and ethnic groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>His aesthetics aren't any more or less derived of those things than his cosmic horror - the dislike of the world arround him it's what inspired the idea of a hopeless humanity. You can't really sepparate the cosmic horror from the idea of unknowable terrors, because the cosmic horror derives from the prevalence of the Outer Gods (a terminology that screams xenophobia more than any tentacled beastie)<br /> <br /> Also, none of what you say disproves that the aesthetic of his creations it's more prevalent that the cosmic horror, it's just baseless ad-hominem (trying to equate the aesthetic with evil)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - Yeah, I know that a bunch of different people expanded his mythos. I'm not knowledgeable on who did what, though. Plus, his work is public domain! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I love the winks to Cthulhu in Conan, I'm not a fan of canonizing Shub-Niggurath looks. There's a difference between creating a story in the Mythos universe and <i>explaining how the mythos &quot;really work&quot;</i> outside Lovecraft original work. And no ad-hominem against the author will change my opinion about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 - Sure, they can challenge the little minions. But as for taking on the big leagues, the only real option is to lull them to sleep and pray to whatever powers are listening that they stay that way. How exactly do you fight against a creature who is so alien to our minds that the very sight of them causes our eyes to explode from their sockets as we are plunged into screaming madness? </div> </div> </div>1\u00ba &quot;little minions&quot;?. Most Lovecraftian monsters aren't cosmic in scale, just aliens and/or old abominations from prehistory that once ruled the earth &quot;and will do once more&quot; . I think you're thinking in the Outer Gods, which comprise a small part of the mythos (you can easily have stories in the Mythos universe without mentioning them).<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba Miskatonic dudes literally shot down the Dunwich Horror after using magic to reveal it's location. But surely that's what you call a &quot;minion&quot;. Cats killed the mosnters of the dark side of the moon that were going to murder Randolph Carter (granted, cats are very magical in the Mythos). But surely those are minions too. By being too focused on the Outer Gods you fail to notice that most Elder Things aren't really of a greater magnitude than such creatures. There's more in Lovecraft than Azathoth (who was mentioned but twice)<br /> <br /> Lovecraft it's pesimistic about humanity's chances, but unspeakable horrors have been defeated time and time again in the mythos. Lovecraft it's pesimistic not because humans are powerless, but because he thinks humans are stupid and base (cats, elegant creatures, are likely to survive us). It's not casual that Armitage it's a head librarian and highly cultured - that's the sort of guy that Lovecraft sees as a &quot;hero&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3\u00ba &quot;that the very sight of them causes our eyes to explode from their sockets as we are plunged into screaming madness&quot; was never the reason of why humanity it's doomed. In fact, this never happens in the whole Lovecraft work, that's a pop culture misconception - Randolph Carter literally saw Yog-Sothoth in it's true form and didn't die of madness nor lost his eyes.<br /> Oh, Carter it's a very special dude, perhaps one of the best and more resorceful dreamers and mages in the Lovecraft universe, and his triffle with the Outer Gods didn't left him unscatched , but Yog wasn't the cause of his downfall, his own hubris caused that.( The Silver Key it's a must read. One of the best books if you want to understand what the Gods really are)<br /> <br /> 4\u00ba Demon it's not situated on the Mythos universe, but all that I'm going to say it's that Earthbounds often come with their own cities from elder times that don't follow the rules of physics, and before waking up they rally people to their side trough nightmares.They're abominable beyond any WoD being, to the point of humans going insane with just their alien looks (no magic involved). Many want to rule the earth like they did in the prehistory.<br /> That's very Lovecraftian (they have a Great Old Ones vive, but they are no Outer Gods) and if your characters weren't themselves inhuman, could lead to a very Lovecraftian storytelling (which it's not the same)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-23-2018, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:19:26-07:00","id":1198702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198689#post1198689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks for clearing it up. I was under the impression that most encounters with the Old Ones result in the individual being driven insane in some fashion or another. As for the subject of minions, Cthulhu technically classifies. He's actually supposed to be a high priest, as opposed to the god he's often portrayed as in modern media. Being a priest would imply that 1) he prays to the Outer Gods, and 2) He preaches their doctrine to fellow worshipers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, my point about comparing them is that we have a general idea of what the Earthbound want and why they want it. But when it comes to Lovecraft, it's mostly ambiguous as to what their long term goals are, or why they're striving towards them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm still leaning towards 'Yes' on picking up the core book and the player's handbook. I'm still on the fence about Earthbound, because DriveThru isn't offering a hardback cover, which is what I prefer to purchase from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:40:11-07:00","id":1198713,"title":"","content":"Earthbound is a pretty slim book, I don't think it would work for a hardback cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:30:44-07:00","id":1198772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thanks for clearing it up. I was under the impression that most encounters with the Old Ones result in the individual being driven insane in some fashion or another. .</div> </div> </div> </div>People that go insane in Lovecraft work are, usually, normal people.<br /> <br /> Most encounters with the Old Ones are normal people facing the supernatural for the first time. Cthulhu was faced (and defeated) by relatively normal people that went insane but most were functional enough to run away and ram the preacher with their boat when &quot;he&quot; was chasing them (which was surprisingly effective).<br /> <br /> &quot;Heroes&quot; that wield supernatural power like Carter or Armitage ain't about to die by just taking a peek on Cthulhu. They may get horrified, but they're made of a stuff that survives the experience. Carter saw much, much, worse (He not only faced but seeked Outer Gods) and was...well...functional most of the time. As an example, after his sense of self was shatered and blown up trough all the universe by Yog, Carter barely lost his jimmies, causing him to make a very serious, but very small, mistake of the kind that someone perfectly sane could have made in a moment of distraction (he forgot the key <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> This is something to keep in mind in Lovecraftian stories whatever the setting. While nobody faces the horror unscatched, there's a difference between normal people and those who eat supernatural for breakfast (say, Mages vs Sleepers in Mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-23-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:34:25-07:00","id":1198778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198348#post1198348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has a good fluff, its mechanics need polish.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also has startlingly bad fluff in a demon mentioning that autistic people have weak connections to their souls and make for easily-had vessels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:38:11-07:00","id":1198782,"title":"","content":"Wow, that's just bad, I must have erased that from memory. Why would the authors feel the need to give a supernatural dimension to autism?. It's the kind of things that just call to be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:09:57-07:00","id":1198791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198782#post1198782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that's just bad, I must have erased that from memory. Why would the authors feel the need to give a supernatural dimension to autism?. It's the kind of things that just call to be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm re-reading it (the beginning of Chapter 4 - it doesn't waste time diving into this), and it's even worse than I recall. Autism is listed as a form of mental illness, for example (page 82). This is after listing the brain dead and people who have had their spirits broken as potential hosts. It'd probably be best for D20 to take an entirely different tack to the issue of inhabitation, such as by simply using a special type of Pact, having the human part at a kind of tug of war with the Fallen, or simply going the Devilman route and having the human part overwhelm the Fallen altogether (or vice versa, in the case of the TV series, but with the demon gaining all of the host's cares). It'd save the readers from having to read another essay on free will and faith when there's the practical matter of subduing a mystical, immaterial entity or being subdued by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T14:24:25-07:00","id":1198843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198778#post1198778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also has startlingly bad fluff in a demon mentioning that autistic people have weak connections to their souls and make for easily-had vessels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, as an autistic person myself (Asperger), I can say from personal experience that we tend to interpret the world quite differently from &quot;normal&quot; people. A lot of things that society puts so much stock in are practically alien concepts for us, because of how our brains work. Conversely, things that 'normal' people consider to be wrong or evil actually make perfect sense from our perspective.<br /> <br /> I'm not a doctor, but I think it would classify as a neurological problem, rather than a psychological one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T05:29:08-07:00","id":1199009,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Demon sure does look interesting, especially as someone who\u2019s been rereading Inferno (nWoD) just awhile ago...<br /> <br /> How much does DtF go into concepts of vice and sin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T06:55:46-07:00","id":1199030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199009#post1199009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much does DtF go into concepts of vice and sin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a lot. It has a morality scale, called torment, which is roughly a bit more polished port of humanity from VtM.<br /> <br /> Generally I can echo that demon is a cool setting, but the mechanics are bad. Personally I handle the lores as minor spheres ala mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:02:51-07:00","id":1199032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199030#post1199030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a lot. It has a morality scale, called torment, which is roughly a bit more polished port of humanity from VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So I have three flavors of Demons to explore from, it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:15:06-07:00","id":1199038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199032#post1199032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. So I have three flavors of Demons to explore from, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate a bit more: Fallen are not even particularily evil at base. They can be good or evil, just like people really, though their (broken) memories of the endless anguish that was the Pit is often driving them towards the evil side of the divinde. That said you could play a character who is more like an angelic being morality wise without issue. Only two of the original legions were evil, one was arguably neutral to good and two were clasically good. The modern factions are of course twisted through the abyss (honestly for my games I ignore their existence completly and deal with demons more on an individual basis rather than trying to make a formal faustian faction or whatever), but most are morally neutral, with one being outright bad and two being at least potentially good, but often severely misguided.<br /> <br /> in DtF you don't play evil demons from hell, you play divine rebels who lost their way, a good portion turning evil along the way and were severly punished, which mentally fucked even the remaining sane ones up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:29:02-07:00","id":1199046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199038#post1199038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To elaborate a bit more: Fallen are not even particularily evil at base. They can be good or evil, just like people really, though their (broken) memories of the endless anguish that was the Pit is often driving them towards the evil side of the divinde. That said you could play a character who is more like an angelic being morality wise without issue. Only two of the original legions were evil, one was arguably neutral to good and two were clasically good. The modern factions are of course twisted through the abyss (honestly for my games I ignore their existence completly and deal with demons more on an individual basis rather than trying to make a formal faustian faction or whatever), but most are morally neutral, with one being outright bad and two being at least potentially good, but often severely misguided.<br /> <br /> in DtF you don't play evil demons from hell, you play divine rebels who lost their way, a good portion turning evil along the way and were severly punished, which mentally fucked even the remaining sane ones up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that I was already aware of. Fallen angels in a Godless world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:43:49-07:00","id":1199052,"title":"","content":"Demon: The Fallen is easily my favorite oWoD game. Even with its flaws (the lore is sometimes a bit odd, the wonky rules here and there and the art that's nothing special) I really like the ideas it brings to the front, and the Fallen can get very powerful. Quick overview of the books:<br /> <br /> Must Have<br /> - The core book, of course. The first four chapters are all lore told in stories instead of matter of factly (which I've been told was pretty common in the late oWoD books).<br /> - Demon Players Guide. The second half of the core book. Has a trove of information for character creation, info on Virtues and Lores, the merits and flaws, DIY Apocalypse Forms as well as rules for relics and rituals.<br /> - Earthbound. Everything you'll need to know about the Earthbound, their origins, their rise and fall as well as rules for creating them and their servants. Also has rules for fighting them.<br /> <br /> Should Have<br /> - Houses of the Fallen. The splatbook for all seven Houses containing lore and has rules for using the Houses. Also has rules for relics and rituals, making it work best with with Players Guide.<br /> - Storytellers Companion. Has lore on the Earthbound (you can ignore this if you have the Earthbound book), the Factions, Greater Demons (who are not really that great tbh), the realm of the dead and rules for interacting with vampires, werewolves, mages, wraiths and hunters.<br /> - Damned and Deceived. The book on Thralls. The first three chapters are all stories from the pov of Thralls (about half the book's length), with the other half being rules for how to make Thrall characters and how to play them, as well as how to find potential Thralls for the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Could Have<br /> - Demon Translation Guide. The go-to book if you want to integrate Fallen and Descent somehow. Has some interesting rules if you want to put Fallen into CofD (1-3 dot Lores become Embeds while 4-5 ones become Exploits) or the other way around, but sadly lack options for the Possessed or its demons.<br /> - City of Angels. Los Angeles is the home city for Demon: The Fallen. It goes into detail about the city, the main movers and shakers as well as the rules for Infernal Courts, which is pretty fun if you really like dynamics along the lines of Camarilla games in Vampire. If neither of those are your groove, you can skip this one.<br /> - Saviours and Destroyers. Like Damned and Deceived but with an even greater perecentage of the book being stories and even less being actual ways to use Exorcists, aka those who hunt Demons. Barely any rules in here and no simple step-by-step character creation with some extra goodies. You might as well skip this, or instead get Hunters Hunted and replace all references to vampires with demons.<br /> <br /> Would Have<br /> - Fear to Tread. A chronicle set in LA. Never run it myself, but as per it nature it's only interesting if you want to run it.<br /> - Days of Fire. What The Book of Nod is to Vampire Days of Fire is to Demon. First 80% is something of a retelling of the story of Creation and the end of the world, as well as references to the other lines. Final 20% is the investigation of the theft of the Dies Ignis parchments, of which Days of Fire is a translation of. Things start to nod add up culmulating in a seemingly impossible double murder. All of this is intercut with signs of the end of the world, including observations of the Red Star.<br /> - World of Darkness: Time of Judgement. The Time of Judgement book for Changeling, Hunter, KotE, Mummy and of course Demon. More or less the sequel for Days of Fire, so make sure you get that as well. Prologue and Epilogue are narrated by Lucifer Morningstar himself, giving some interesting insights and a line near the end that will uproot everything you thought you knew about the game. The three scenarios for Demon can be summed up as Fallen VS Earthbound, Fallen &amp; Greater Demons VS Earthbound and Fallen &amp; Lucifer VS Earthbound, the latter of which being the most interesting and playing to the central theme of Demon the most. I'd almost say get this just for the Lucifer parts, but most of the book you'll never use for Demon.<br /> - Trilogy of the Fallen. A fiction trilogy written by Greg Stolze. From what I've heard the first is pretty good, but the second less so. Get it if you want to read some fiction on Demon.<br /> - Lucifer's Shadow. An anthology of ten short stories. No idea about the quality.<br /> <br /> And finally, there's Dark Ages - Devil's Due. It's a Dark Ages book on pacts between mortals and demons, and while it's not related to Demon: The Fallen it shares a lot of ideas and mechanics (some of which it even does better). I haven't read all of it yet but from what I've seen it's pretty neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:07:15-07:00","id":1199061,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I don't have the budget to buy crap loads of books associated with particular game lines. Which is why I decided to go for the 20th anniversary editions of Vampire and Changeling. Plus, there's enough coverage about the games elsewhere that I can get a general run through of the game's fluff if I need it. Sadly, Demon the Fallen does not have this, which is why I was curious about it. If there were a D20 that had all the important mechanics, then that would be great. But as it stands now, I've only got the core book and the player's guide on my wish list.<br /> <br /> <br /> So far, I'm liking the sound of it, even if it does seem to be part of a niche play style. I also really like the concept of the demons not being necessarily evil, but rather misunderstood. We've always been lead to believe that demons were the incarnation of evil itself. But there's two sides to every story, and we rarely prove willing to hear them out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2018, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:26:55-07:00","id":1199067,"title":"","content":"What I found interesting after reading Demon the Fallen when it came out was the idea that the Fallen's personality can be unpredictable to their peers. The evilest most desperate and hateful Demon could possess a serial killer and wind up with a Fallen who is jarred by the mortality of even someone so despicable and combined with eons of loneliness in the Abyss you could have the resulting character be someone realizing humanity for the first time and seek redemption and compassion. Conversely you could have one of the more sympathetic and merciful fallen possess a kind selfless person and have it result in a psychotic nihilistic Fallen due to some strange interaction experiencing human memories and the hate and loathing and hypocrisy could just erupt. In the Novels Fallen seemed really careful around other Demons particularly ones they knew from before the Abyss. It was like they had no idea that possessing a human body and mind and countless ages in isolation could reshuffle someones priorities and personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:49:53-07:00","id":1199072,"title":"","content":"Generally I can say that those people who play demon tend to like it alot. But it usually takes a bit of houseruling to cope with the system. But the setting is great and very evocative, combining many things from different wod gamelines (the fight for the future or mage, the reconciliating with what you are from vampire, the fight for existence itself from werewolf, etc).<br /> <br /> That said here is what, in my mind, seperates DtF from other gamelines. Other splats hide from humanity, wether out of self interest (most) or due to metaphysical complications (mages, werewolfs). Demons don't. While they can in minor ways be fucked over by disbelief (though very very minorly compared to mages and easily overcome by burning a bit of fuel unless they've been trained to negate lores... which is part of one of their apocalypse scenarios but I'm getting off track) they generally don't care if people know about them. They are in fact empowered by it. One of their ways of gaining Faith (their fuel) is to reveal themselves to mortals. They build cults around themselves. Sure so far no one has gone on national television, but that's more because it'd place a target on their chest. Demons will reveal themselves (and everything else along with them) to humanity sooner or later. The big metaplot event of demon was Lucifer himself showing up over LA, visible for miles and making hundreds of thousands of people aware of his existence. And all the bigshots in hell when they come out will want to do similar things, to build big cults, to get much faith etc. pp. This is also excerbated by the fact that humans (and in fact most beings) cant really lastingly hurt demons. Loosing your host really sucks, but the demon usually survives, unless another demons eats them (or a mage if you want them to exist in your demon games does some high level rote I guess).<br /> <br /> So demon is an apocalyptic game. You're on earth. Millions and millons of more demons will come to earth soon, some of them very very potent (not so much mechanically actually, but thats easily fixed by giving them the Mastery trait Earthbounds have). They will tear the earth apart, some of them because that's their goals, others because they clash in their objectives. Earth will never be the same again. Maybe it'll take just a year, maybe ten. Where is Lucifer? Can he stop this? Can we prevent this? Do we even want to? And if we do what do we want to build from the ashes of civilization?<br /> <br /> Demon is one of the most high powered WoD games. While you can do slice of life stuff with demons just trying to adjust, the setting is set up in a away that very much has the apocalypse impending and cosmic consequences could very well be the end game of your chronicle. This is a game of angels and demons clashing in the sky over cities, the old gods awakening, not bloodsuckers trying to hide from the herd they tell themselves is inferior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:56:57-07:00","id":1199073,"title":"","content":"The whole identity crisis thing and the cosmic scale of the setting also reminds me of Mummy the Curse. For me, who apparently found hardly anything wrong with the CofD games published so far, that's a good sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:51:06-07:00","id":1199096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198778#post1198778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also has startlingly bad fluff in a demon mentioning that autistic people have weak connections to their souls and make for easily-had vessels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that the severely impaired are not difficult to mentally/spiritually displace by a monster like a demon, not 'if you are on the spectrum God hates you and a devourer will eat your soul.'<br /> <br /> As far as fictional possessions go, I don't see much categorical difference between catatonic autism and brain damage. Seems okay to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:56:14-07:00","id":1199232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199096#post1199096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the idea is that the severely impaired are not difficult to mentally/spiritually displace by a monster like a demon, not 'if you are on the spectrum God hates you and a devourer will eat your soul.'<br /> <br /> As far as fictional possessions go, I don't see much categorical difference between catatonic autism and brain damage. Seems okay to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I believe that's what they were trying to say as well. Such people lacking the spiritual or mental fortitude to resist possession, rather than being predisposed to attracting it. Doesn't sound offensive to me, but rather a practical solution to Demons in need of a host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:58:05-07:00","id":1199234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199072#post1199072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Millions and millons of more demons will come to earth soon</div> </div> </div> </div>Two million, two thousand, two hundred and four. That's the exact number of Fallen. Minus the 666 Earthbound, all of them are on Earth. There might still be a few somewhere in the Underworld, since they didn't escape before collapsing the thing. That might mean that Charon (the original one was a Fallen, and specifically NOT the same Charon of Wraith fame) and his few allies are still around. That might also mean that they are the ones that lie at the center of the Labyrinth. This might also mean that Charon has become the Underworld equivalent of an Earthbound, which is all sorts of terrifying. Oh, and while on the subject of Wraith... you know Nhudri, the inventor of Soulforging? Well, let's just say that there was once a Malefactor by the name of Nhudriel working closely at the side of Charon (the Fallen) and created the first lanterns that would later be copied by the Ferrymen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199072#post1199072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a game of angels and demons clashing in the sky over cities, the old gods awakening, not bloodsuckers trying to hide from the herd they tell themselves is inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It feels greater than the issues of Vampires, something that is grander than the cosmologies of Werewolf and Mage and the issues of Changelings feel... trite of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:05:53-07:00","id":1199238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199072#post1199072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said here is what, in my mind, separates DtF from other gamelines. Other splats hide from humanity, wether out of self interest (most) or due to metaphysical complications (mages, werewolfs). Demons don't. While they can in minor ways be fucked over by disbelief (though very very minorly compared to mages and easily overcome by burning a bit of fuel unless they've been trained to negate lores... which is part of one of their apocalypse scenarios but I'm getting off track) they generally don't care if people know about them. They are in fact empowered by it. One of their ways of gaining Faith (their fuel) is to reveal themselves to mortals. They build cults around themselves. Sure so far no one has gone on national television, but that's more because it'd place a target on their chest. Demons will reveal themselves (and everything else along with them) to humanity sooner or later. The big metaplot event of demon was Lucifer himself showing up over LA, visible for miles and making hundreds of thousands of people aware of his existence. And all the big shots in hell when they come out will want to do similar things, to build big cults, to get much faith etc. pp. This is also exacerbated by the fact that humans (and in fact most beings) cant really lastingly hurt demons. Loosing your host really sucks, but the demon usually survives, unless another demons eats them (or a mage if you want them to exist in your demon games does some high level rote I guess).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I used to think Changeling had a similar premise, given that their very existence is sustained by humanity's belief in what they symbolize or represent in the world. The fact that they created the Changeling Way ritual as a last resort option to survive Banality (and that many of them still resent having to use it) kind of supported my preconception.<br /> <br /> I just figured that The Mists were the main reason why they don't (i.e <i>can't</i>) go around exposing themselves in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:36:05-07:00","id":1199250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199234#post1199234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two million, two thousand, two hundred and four. That's the exact number of Fallen. Minus the 666 Earthbound, all of them are on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc 100 million Elohim were created in the beginning, two thirds of which rebelled. The War of Wrath killed a third of all Elohim. So outh of 66.6 million demons originally, there should be 44.4 million out there total. In the end it makes little difference. Wether 2 or 44 million demons, that many supernatural beings showing up (with their powerlevel) is bound to fuck things up. The setting assumes so far only a few have escaped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There might still be a few somewhere in the Underworld, since they didn't escape before collapsing the thing. That might mean that Charon (the original one was a Fallen, and specifically NOT the same Charon of Wraith fame) and his few allies are still around. That might also mean that they are the ones that lie at the center of the Labyrinth. This might also mean that Charon has become the Underworld equivalent of an Earthbound, which is all sorts of terrifying. </div> </div> </div>Well let's just say that Elohim were created at the dawn of time, they were never born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T17:09:10-07:00","id":1199259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199250#post1199250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc 100 million Elohim were created in the beginning, two thirds of which rebelled. The War of Wrath killed a third of all Elohim. So outh of 66.6 million demons originally, there should be 44.4 million out there total. In the end it makes little difference. Wether 2 or 44 million demons, that many supernatural beings showing up (with their powerlevel) is bound to fuck things up. The setting assumes so far only a few have escaped.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that 2 million Fallen on 7.2 billion humans would be about 1 Fallen per 3600 people, and if there's 44 million of them that would be 1 Fallen per 164 people. That's quite the difference, and even then that would make them the second most populous of all splats aside from Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T17:17:13-07:00","id":1199260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199250#post1199250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc 100 million Elohim were created in the beginning, two thirds of which rebelled. The War of Wrath killed a third of all Elohim. So outh of 66.6 million demons originally, there should be 44.4 million out there total. In the end it makes little difference. Wether 2 or 44 million demons, that many supernatural beings showing up (with their powerlevel) is bound to fuck things up. The setting assumes so far only a few have escaped.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The setting also assumes that only <b>the weakest</b> demons managed to escape. The heavy hitters are still trapped in Hell, waiting for somebody to set them loose upon the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1