waiting for somebody to set them loose upon the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ha, tell that to Belial the Great Beast and the Archdukes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:24:02-07:00","id":1199317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199312#post1199312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ha, tell that to Belial the Great Beast and the Archdukes</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought they were <i>summoned</i>, not escaped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:38:20-07:00","id":1199323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen#post1198332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while I have zero interest in Descent (I don't care for the God Machine idea, and even less so for a game that revolves around it), I have been curious about Fallen for some time. Unfortunately, I seem to be getting mixed reviews about its themes and mechanics. Some people think it's good and are hoping for a D20 release, while others weren't too pleased with it, judging by how we don't even have a forum dedicated to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have zero interest in Descent. I don't like the gnostic elements or the whole &quot;God Machine idea&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say Yay. It's a great setting, even if the mechanics deserve a revision (I'd love a Demon &quot;D20&quot; edition).<br /> <br /> With some work you can always adapt the rules according your own experience (but it requires some experience with the game, of course).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen#post1198332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some have said that players weren't happy about it adhering primarily to Abrahamic faiths, but that's something I'm not really worried about. Vampire kind of already did that by incorporating the biblical God into the vampire origin story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It runs ok within my own WoD. I like the whole Abrahamic mythology thing (I completely ignored the metaphysics of other game lines, and developed my own coherence using the Vampire-Demon-Wraith lore).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen#post1198332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others have said the game doesn't really allow for cross faction groups, which is also something I'm not too worried about. I mean, I have yet to see a game where people are playing Camarilla / Sabbat in the same coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>It allows. Having a gang of Fallen with diverging political views is not very different from having a group of humans with different political views (unless they're hysterical about their own views, of course). I'm a conservative Catholic that abhors most (if not all) modern social views and I have both libertarian and leftist friends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen#post1198332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, what I am concerned with is that there is barely any coverage surrounding this game, both in youtube videos and wikis as well. They just sort of skim through the game without giving an in depth look about its premise or setting. This makes me hesitant about buying it, since I don't like the idea of paying for a game I know almost nothing about and finding out later that it's not right for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but the game is really well written, and the fiction if quite immersive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T01:05:21-07:00","id":1199326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199323#post1199323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It allows. Having a gang of Fallen with diverging political views is not very different from having a group of humans with different political views (unless they're hysterical about their own views, of course). I'm a conservative Catholic that abhors most (if not all) modern social views and I have both libertarian and leftist friends.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find that a little bit hard to believe when some of the factions have radically different ideologies and goals. I can see Faustians and Cryptics working together, since one faction seeks to garner knowledge, and the other seeks to foster humanity's divine potential. But then you've got Raveners who just want to destroy the universe, the Reconcilers who want to earn God's forgiveness, and the Luciferans who are planning to launch another rebellion once they track down their missing leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not too worried about it, since it's something that's appeared in other games before. And running a game where everybody has at least some common goal to work towards would probably make running a group much easier than having everybody trying to tear each other apart from the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2018, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T01:41:18-07:00","id":1199329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199326#post1199326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I find that a little bit hard to believe when some of the factions have radically different ideologies and goals. I can see Faustians and Cryptics working together, since one faction seeks to garner knowledge, and the other seeks to foster humanity's divine potential. But then you've got Raveners who just want to destroy the universe, the Reconcilers who want to earn God's forgiveness, and the Luciferans who are planning to launch another rebellion once they track down their missing leader.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The question is how dedicated to faction politics they are. It is possible that the main story doesn't revolve around one faction goal and different fallen may put their differences aside to deal with...whatever. Faustians, Cryptics and Luciferans usually work together without too many problems (unless you have fanatics). Reconcilers work without too much hassle aswell, as long no Luciferans are around, though others may think of them as a bit pathetic. Raveners only work together with Raveners.<br /> <br /> That said as noted before I never found too much use for the factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T04:40:17-07:00","id":1199344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199326#post1199326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that a little bit hard to believe when some of the factions have radically different ideologies and goals. I can see Faustians and Cryptics working together, since one faction seeks to garner knowledge, and the other seeks to foster humanity's divine potential. But then you've got Raveners who just want to destroy the universe, the Reconcilers who want to earn God's forgiveness, and the Luciferans who are planning to launch another rebellion once they track down their missing leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not too worried about it, since it's something that's appeared in other games before. And running a game where everybody has at least some common goal to work towards would probably make running a group much easier than having everybody trying to tear each other apart from the inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> wrote. The characters don't need to be firebrands.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T07:37:28-07:00","id":1199362,"title":"","content":"Personally I think Hsien (from which Demon shamelessly copies ALL mechanics) is a much more interesting game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T07:55:12-07:00","id":1199371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199362#post1199362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think Hsien (from which Demon shamelessly copies ALL mechanics) is a much more interesting game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm assuming you mean the Hsien listed in the back of C20? Those guys do look like fun, but I know virtually nothing about the Asian culture and wouldn't be able to portray them accurately at all.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I've got that problem a lot when it comes to foreign settings / characters in the World of Darkness. There's lots of settings and character types I'd love to try out, but I simply don't know how to play them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199323#post1199323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I also have zero interest in Descent. I don't like the gnostic elements or the whole &quot;God Machine idea&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thing is, I wouldn't have minded GMC or Descent if they were their own separate universe, as I'm getting strong Shin Megami vibes off it. But as part of the Chronicles of Darkness, I don't like it. The premise comes across as too much science fiction and not enough supernatural. Fallen is much closer to what I was looking for when I heard about a game allowing us to play as actual Demons.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T01:57:55-07:00","id":1199639,"title":"","content":"\u201cThe Unchained from Descent are not the demons I expected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Unchained from Descent are no true demons.\u201d<br /> <br /> One of these is something I fully understand. The other is just plain sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:45:45-07:00","id":1199672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199639#post1199639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThe Unchained from Descent are not the demons I expected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Unchained from Descent are no true demons.\u201d<br /> <br /> One of these is something I fully understand. The other is just plain sad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I said, I get strong Shin Megami vibes from Descent.<br /> <br /> Demons, Angels and Deities in the Shin Megami series are portrayed from a more technological view point than a supernatural one. There's a downloadable app for your smart phone that allows you to summon Demons, Angels and even Gods to fight for you in battle. There's also multiple references that suggest the entire universe is just one big program that YHVH managed to seize control over. He managed to cast down all the other deities by manipulating humans into applying their power of comprehension upon them. By assigning the gods with forms and personalities, they became less than what they were, which was originally forces of nature at one with the universe itself. Only YHVH managed to escape this fate, because he did his best to avoid direct interaction with mortals. Without being able to apply comprehension to him, YHVH retained his existence as an all powerful being who exists everywhere around us. When he has to interact with the world of mortals, he sends Angels to serve as proxy agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-26-2018, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:55:08-07:00","id":1199678,"title":"","content":"I think the point most people try to get across is the technological aspect is really just a thin coat of paint around the core aspect. It isnt really difficult to 'paint' it all differently.<br /> Now you've said your not fond of the gnostic aspect of the game (which is what the core aspect is) so you not wanting to play the game for that reason is perfectly valid in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As for DtFallen, i've read it but never played it. What really interested me in the concept was that you had these very powerful beings (angels, then demons) that could do pretty much anything, but they've never been weak and human. Becoming that is absolutely world changing for these beings and you can get creative with the responses to that.<br /> <br /> I hope you can have a game running and you have fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:02:44-07:00","id":1199683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199678#post1199678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for DtFallen, i've read it but never played it. What really interested me in the concept was that you had these very powerful beings (angels, then demons) that could do pretty much anything, but they've never been weak and human. Becoming that is absolutely world changing for these beings and you can get creative with the responses to that.<br /> <br /> I hope you can have a game running and you have fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same story with Changeling, actually. Except I would imagine that Changeling has a (somewhat) more lighthearted tone to it than Demon.<br /> <br /> Death of the Dreaming, while obviously tragic, sounds less menacing than the death of the entire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:55:29-07:00","id":1199700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199672#post1199672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As I said, I get strong Shin Megami vibes from Descent.<br /> <br /> Demons, Angels and Deities in the Shin Megami series are portrayed from a more technological view point than a supernatural one. There's a downloadable app for your smart phone that allows you to summon Demons, Angels and even Gods to fight for you in battle. There's also multiple references that suggest the entire universe is just one big program that YHVH managed to seize control over. He managed to cast down all the other deities by manipulating humans into applying their power of comprehension upon them. By assigning the gods with forms and personalities, they became less than what they were, which was originally forces of nature at one with the universe itself. Only YHVH managed to escape this fate, because he did his best to avoid direct interaction with mortals. Without being able to apply comprehension to him, YHVH retained his existence as an all powerful being who exists everywhere around us. When he has to interact with the world of mortals, he sends Angels to serve as proxy agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the vibes are there. Must be a cultural thing, then, for people (like us) to draw different conclusions about where Descent stands. <br /> <br /> Now, returning to the Fallen - I\u2019m tempted to run them as \u201cthe old ones of the world before\u201d trope, perhaps a bit more than the literal angel &amp; demon trope. As in, the Ancient Ones and the Old Gods who came back to reclaim the world. That\u2019s still possible, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:09:37-07:00","id":1199705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199700#post1199700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the vibes are there. Must be a cultural thing, then, for people (like us) to draw different conclusions about where Descent stands.<br /> <br /> Now, returning to the Fallen - I\u2019m tempted to run them as \u201cthe old ones of the world before\u201d trope, perhaps a bit more than the literal angel &amp; demon trope. As in, the Ancient Ones and the Old Gods who came back to reclaim the world. That\u2019s still possible, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From what I've been able to glean together, Fallen does state that some Demons used to be worshiped as gods by humanity. However, I think most of them became Earthbound, rather than being cast into Hell with the rest of them.<br /> <br /> So yes, that is an approach you can take for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:13:24-07:00","id":1199706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199705#post1199705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> From what I've been able to glean together, Fallen does state that some Demons used to be worshiped as gods by humanity. However, I think most of them became Earthbound, rather than being cast into Hell with the rest of them.<br /> <br /> So yes, that is an approach you can take for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Great. Now my headcanon of the WoD being the Time Before from Awakening is settled. The Elohim will be there, in the deepest reaches of both the Supernal and the Abyss, saying \u201cDammit, now we <i>literally</i> broke the world, and we still don\u2019t know where God and Lucifer are.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:56:41-07:00","id":1199744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199706#post1199706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great. Now my headcanon of the WoD being the Time Before from Awakening is settled. The Elohim will be there, in the deepest reaches of both the Supernal and the Abyss, saying \u201cDammit, now we <i>literally</i> broke the world, and we still don\u2019t know where God and Lucifer are.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My headcanon for the end of the world scenario is that the Abrahamic God is actually being overthrown. The supernatural heavy hitters band together and conduct an all out rebellion against him and his creations, which culminates in the destruction of most of the known world. When the dust settles, those who remain go about picking up the pieces and starting things over the way they should have been. A new era of magic begins and the world no longer favors human supremacy, as the supernatural races are once again free to openly reveal themselves, instead of hiding behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-26-2018, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:58:33-07:00","id":1199782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199705#post1199705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> From what I've been able to glean together, Fallen does state that some Demons used to be worshiped as gods by humanity. However, I think most of them became Earthbound, rather than being cast into Hell with the rest of them.<br /> <br /> So yes, that is an approach you can take for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> All Fallen were thrown into the Abyss/Hell. The ones that were Earthbound were summoned in ancient times thanks to Lucifer stepping in to get his lieutenants back and then humans repeating until a total of 666 earthbound came to be IIRC. Unfortunately they turned out to be completely batshit bonkers and weren't made any better by possessing physical objects(it just made them worse). The only Fallen to ever escape being thrown into the Abyss would be Charon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:16:08-07:00","id":1199790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199782#post1199782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All Fallen were thrown into the Abyss/Hell. The ones that were Earthbound were summoned in ancient times thanks to Lucifer stepping in to get his lieutenants back and then humans repeating until a total of 666 earthbound came to be IIRC. Unfortunately they turned out to be completely batshit bonkers and weren't made any better by possessing physical objects(it just made them worse). The only Fallen to ever escape being thrown into the Abyss would be Charon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that Charon avoided being thrown into the Abyss rather than escaped it, but the place he's in now is pretty much the Abyss in its own right. And Nhudri of course, who might very well be Nhudriel, one of Charon's (the Fallen, not the Wraith) old companions who got stuck in there as well. That would mean that Nhudriel somehow avoided going insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T20:32:11-07:00","id":1199932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199312#post1199312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha, tell that to Belial the Great Beast and the Archdukes</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I don't like about the game is the Archdukes being permanent residents of Earth rather than Hell. Were I to run one I think I'd have their summonings have turned out to be of limited duration due to the strain of containing such powerful spirits in reliquaries, or Lucifer having been able to undo them and banish them back into the abyss once he realized his lieutenants' changed natures.<br /> <br /> I prefer those great powers of darkness at a remove, only able to affect events in the world of the living through proxies or in rare cases if grand summoning rituals give them brief access. It also allows for the possibility of them using pacts to drag human souls down to Hell among them and their fellows, when such spirits were never meant to go there\u2014aligning with the mythology and cautionary tales of devil's bargains (not to mention the nature of infernalism in other game lines).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T02:15:19-07:00","id":1199966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199790#post1199790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more that Charon avoided being thrown into the Abyss rather than escaped it, but the place he's in now is pretty much the Abyss in its own right. And Nhudri of course, who might very well be Nhudriel, one of Charon's (the Fallen, not the Wraith) old companions who got stuck in there as well. That would mean that Nhudriel somehow avoided going insane.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah true. He avoided it by fleeing deep into the underworld where the loyal host couldn't follow because they knew nothing about the place. Possibly a smart move, possibly not. I suppose it'd depend on the GM what happened to him unless white wolf/onyx path ever addresses it somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T15:36:47-07:00","id":1200242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1199932#post1199932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I don't like about the game is the Archdukes being permanent residents of Earth rather than Hell. Were I to run one I think I'd have their summonings have turned out to be of limited duration due to the strain of containing such powerful spirits in reliquaries, or Lucifer having been able to undo them and banish them back into the abyss once he realized his lieutenants' changed natures.<br /> <br /> I prefer those great powers of darkness at a remove, only able to affect events in the world of the living through proxies or in rare cases if grand summoning rituals give them brief access. It also allows for the possibility of them using pacts to drag human souls down to Hell among them and their fellows, when such spirits were never meant to go there\u2014aligning with the mythology and cautionary tales of devil's bargains (not to mention the nature of infernalism in other game lines).</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the rules in the Storytellers Companion the ritual for summoning an Archduke, if linear with the other rituals, would look something like this:<br /> <br /> Difficulty: 10, True Name only.<br /> Minimum Successes: 60<br /> Minimum Faith Points: 600<br /> Special Conditions: 10+<br /> Reliquary Faith Potential: N/A (the reliquaries of the Earthbound had Lucifer involved, remember)<br /> Mortal Faith Potential: 5+<br /> <br /> If not far more of course, or if it's limited to ST Fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T21:48:40-07:00","id":1200347,"title":"","content":"I've made a demon, haven't played it yet, I'd easily say it's the most fun I've ever had actually making a character for what it's worth. Can't wait to find a chance to use it. I found the rules understandable and will probably play it mixed in with other WoD games as we tend to do now.<br /> (Also made a changeling lawyer I want to playone day. Making WoD Charatcers is just too addictive.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23892-damienls","name":"DamienLS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23892_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T04:23:55-07:00","id":1201204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DamienLS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1200347#post1200347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made a demon, haven't played it yet, I'd easily say it's the most fun I've ever had actually making a character for what it's worth. Can't wait to find a chance to use it. I found the rules understandable and will probably play it mixed in with other WoD games as we tend to do now.<br /> (Also made a changeling lawyer I want to playone day. Making WoD Charatcers is just too addictive.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Mixing it in with the other games is what I find quite fun. Especially when playing the first house angel that is essentially the embodiment of stars(which includes the sun) and then having vampires talk about the sun burning them up. That was an amusing moment hah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:08:08-07:00","id":1201289,"title":"","content":"Do note that the rules for making Pacts are pretty solid on their own, but if you start adding books other than the core book you'll be running into some silly stuff. If you use the Players Guide you gain access to Merits, which you can buy with Freebie Points. This allows for all sorts of shenanigans, including being able to buy the Independent Income merit which is the Resources Background without the need for work. And since the rules specify you can't buy Backgrounds with points from Pacts this is the way to go. Then there's when you use Damned and Deceived, where if you use its rules to make Thralls you can technically increase their Faith Potential buy spending 7 points per dot, which can let you turn a Thrall into quite the Faith cow.<br /> <br /> Of course, no Storyteller worth their salt would allow either of those, but it's a fun little detail. Even when going by the core book alone you can up someone's Willpower to 10 by spending a few points on it and still have enough of them to spend elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T03:36:05-07:00","id":1202512,"title":"","content":"If I ran Demon:<br /> <br /> - I would take Mage players, and give Demons Spheres. It seems thematically appropriate for Demons to control the world with a Sphere system, and furthermore in the Demon lore Avatars are just Angels/Demon corpses that humans are using to bend reality. So in terms of fluff and crunch it's neat.<br /> <br /> - I feel like I would need to change most of the setting and the goals of Demons, and change what a Demon is.<br /> <br /> RPing a Demon who has escaped from hell, but has a lot of Amnesia, and was never human to begin with... well it's just so strange. Wraiths, Werewolves, Changelings, Mages, they are all human in some sense. Even Chatterlings and Revenents have common ties to the players, who can comprehend them. Angels and Demons? It's just so... Think about it like this. If you play Fomori: Freak Legion, you play as the Fomorus, the human possessed by a Bane. You don't play as the Bane. Bane's are incomprehensible to us.<br /> <br /> I think about Demon the same way. These Demons have escaped from hell and need a host, something they can grow strong and recover their memories inside. This is almost always a Human. The resulting combination is a synthesis of the two forms. The &quot;fleshbound&quot; Demon is the power and spirit, and driving force, the awakening, while the human being who is the vessel is what we relate to and understand.<br /> <br /> The Fleshbound need their host in the short and mid term. If their Host dies, they have to find a new one, and in the process they have to pass some difficult rolls or lose memories (Lore) or Willpower. It's hassle, but the Demon doesn't truly *need* the host in the long-term, if you see what I mean.<br /> <br /> The equivalent of Arete is Lore; the rating which represents how much your Demon has remembered. At Lore 6 they understand what they were for, giving you Exploding 10s for all thematically related Sphere rolls.<br /> <br /> - I would finally change the goals and ideas of Demons and their Hosts. The general consensus is that a Demonic uprising, apocalypse or Gehenna would be a bad thing. The overarching theme is watching for signs of the endtimes and doing your absolute best to shift fate. Naturally there are infernalists and Fleshbound who long for the rapture, and who work to bring it sooner.<br /> <br /> - Furthermore, Earthbound use soil and buildings and powerful objects for a reason. Demons are corrosive and can burn through weak hosts. So Fleshbound need to struggle to stay alive. They can't stay still or they will die, essentially. They are only able to prolong their existence by increasing an inversion of the Lore rating, their Host rating. The stronger their Host rating, the harder it is to suppress or remove the Demon with the Spirit Sphere, True Faith etc. and the less the Demon inside them damages their body. The idea is that Hosts need to be active in the world, because unless they take risks, make bargains and work with other Demons, gather faith etc. they won't be able to survive the corrosive force inside of them. Host rating would also apply to channeling the power of your Demon; taking an Apocalyptic form is cool, but if you do it for more turns than you have Host, you will start to take Aggravated damage from the burnout. Embodying an Attribute from your Demon is useful, but you can't raise any Attribute higher than your Host rating through this method. You get the idea.<br /> <br /> - So a major theme would be Demon and Host as parasites, allies and enemies. The Demon has no choice but to let the Host use its Spheres and its Lore rating, but the Demon does have its own Attributes and Abilities and Merits and Flaws. The Demon gains EXP at the same rate as the Host, and it will increase its Lore rating when it can afford it, unless it has a good reason not to. And if their Lore exceeds your Host rating, then you are going to start slowly dying. If your Demon decides it is better off without you, then it is going to stop trying to protect you, and it's going to seek to burn through your body so it can find a new Host. In that case you had better find a way to one-up it and shift the power balance of the relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-03-2018, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:04:06-07:00","id":1202696,"title":"","content":"YAY! I think Demon gets a bad rap.<br /> <br /> First off, I'm an atheist. Demon's backstory is no more real to me than any other fantasy or mythological tale. Despite the fact that I've never associated myself with any religion, even as a child, I have always associated demons with Paradise Lost. So for me, there was no other option for the foundation of DTF.<br /> <br /> I also do not see DTF as inherently Christian. If anything, at best, it's Abrahamic, which links it to Judaism, Christianity, and Islam, but even then, that's looking at things backwards. The basic setup of Demon is Paradise Lost, but Paradise Lost isn't about Moses, Jesus, or Muhammad. The story predates the entire concept of prophets and holy books.<br /> <br /> The way I make sense of things is, the backstory in DTF happened. Then the Fallen were thrown in the Abyss and sealed away. The world then continued to form and evolve. Human ended up being caught in the middle of a tug of war between pretty much every supernatural faction ever created. Most of the religions of the world, including Christianity, were influenced or in some cases outright created by uber powerful beings, such as the Earthbound, Lucifer, Methuselahs, and the like. Lucifer promoted, if not outright created, Christianity to combat the Earthbound who relied on peganism.<br /> <br /> So I don't think DTF says 'Christians are right.' None of the backstory of DTF is in the Old Testement, New Testement, or the Quran. In the World of Darkness, those religions have pieces of the puzzle at best.<br /> <br /> Also, if you really wanted to strip all that way, you could completely remove the stuff about the War in Heaven and have Demons have no memory of the time before the Abyss. Or create your own backstory. It's a pretty adaptable set up. You could easily take the WtA or Mage cosmology and fit Demon into it.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that these represent only my own personal opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24088,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","user":"thespiraleffect","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:36:57-07:00","id":1202711,"title":"","content":"As I said, I'm not overly concerned about the idea of the game focused around Abrahamic dogma. I'd personally choose that kind of setting over the hyper advanced technology from Descent.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, I'm actually very intrigued by the idea of playing one of the rebellious angels, because it's a bold and fresh idea. The only other game I can think of where you blatantly rebel against the Abrahamic God himself is Shin Megami, but that universe is more closely inspired by Descent.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can understand the public backlash from outsiders who look at the game's premise and consider it extremely blasphemous. But as somebody who's renounced Christianity (twice, I might add) then tried to establish my own cult in high school, I don't really care about being labeled a heretic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T01:07:47-07:00","id":1202901,"title":"","content":"Its not like you have to treat The Creator as the abrahamic god either. I certainly didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:40:46-07:00","id":1203397,"title":"","content":"On this subject though, it seems entirely plausible you can easily end up playing Angel:the Redemption as some like to call it. Nothing forces you to be evil and torment isn't necessarily friendly towards your spells. I like the fact that it seems the game can go either way.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I'm also an atheist, but I did notice a lot of butt hurt individuals wanted more types of demons like Asian and such, but that seems like way too much for one book so I don't think Christians were the only vocal protesters. We'd end up with another 5 books to detail each pantheon. &gt;_&lt; No thanks. Having entirely read through demon though, I hope the get around to D20. It could use a little house cleaning and get the errata added in. So my final verdict would be wait and see if they get us DtF 20 before actually buying. <br /> <br /> SMT is so great for nailing that atmosphere sometimes. I need to get more of them under my belt. I'd also say there are more JRPGs with similar theme but it's hard to recall which. Wasn't there an FF where you fight god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23892-damienls","name":"DamienLS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23892_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T07:12:46-07:00","id":1203404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DamienLS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203397#post1203397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this subject though, it seems entirely plausible you can easily end up playing Angel:the Redemption as some like to call it. Nothing forces you to be evil and torment isn't necessarily friendly towards your spells. I like the fact that it seems the game can go either way.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I'm also an atheist, but I did notice a lot of butt hurt individuals wanted more types of demons like Asian and such, but that seems like way too much for one book so I don't think Christians were the only vocal protesters. We'd end up with another 5 books to detail each pantheon. &gt;_&lt; No thanks. Having entirely read through demon though, I hope the get around to D20. It could use a little house cleaning and get the errata added in. So my final verdict would be wait and see if they get us DtF 20 before actually buying.<br /> <br /> SMT is so great for nailing that atmosphere sometimes. I need to get more of them under my belt. I'd also say there are more JRPGs with similar theme but it's hard to recall which. Wasn't there an FF where you fight god?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was actually thinking of trying out a Faustian who attempts to create a new paradise on earth. Less out of a desire to repent for his hand in the rebellion and more out of the interest of spiting God. He wants to prove that mortals are perfectly capable of being happy without God's influence.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's the fact he's been tormented in Hell for the last several thousand years, and his interpretation of paradise may have become a little skewed by that experience. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> The closest I can think of is Final Fantasy 6, who's final boss battle is pretty much meant to symbolize the ascent from Hell, to Purgatory, to Heaven, and finally challenging God, himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T07:36:47-07:00","id":1203410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203404#post1203404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I was actually thinking of trying out a Faustian who attempts to create a new paradise on earth. Less out of a desire to repent for his hand in the rebellion and more out of the interest of spiting God. He wants to prove that mortals are perfectly capable of being happy without God's influence.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's the fact he's been tormented in Hell for the last several thousand years, and his interpretation of paradise may have become a little skewed by that experience. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> The closest I can think of is Final Fantasy 6, who's final boss battle is pretty much meant to symbolize the ascent from Hell, to Purgatory, to Heaven, and finally challenging God, himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it. I love it so much. Sounds like a good ole time for sure. I made a Luciferian Devil who ended up in the body of a preacher's daughter and wants to continue the good fight to impress Lucifer when he returns one day. So I see similar goals here. I haven't put the finishing touches on her though because I need her to be able to mix with V20 characters and rules because I don't want an entire party of demons. I'd have to teach everyone how to play them. After teaching them Vampire the hard way I don't feel like it again. Good luck though. I hope you achieve greatness.<br /> <br /> Ah, yeah, that's what I was thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23892-damienls","name":"DamienLS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23892_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T09:49:03-07:00","id":1203437,"title":"","content":"I've renounced Christianity and I am a Classical Greco-Roman Pagan (I used to be an atheist before that) but I utterly despise Demon: The Fallen for many reasons.<br /> <br /> The chief reasons being the fact that WW proposed Demon's cosmology as the &quot;One True Way&quot; cosmology for the World of Darkness for a while. The fact that it depends on the Revised Edition metaplot (which I also strongly dislike) doesn't help matters either.<br /> <br /> Then there's the material found in the Earthbound book that basically states that the evil Earthbound invented Paganism, which is eerily similar to the whole &quot;Pagan Gods are actually evil Demons&quot; argument that a lot of fundamentalist Christians put forward, and that I have had to put up with in real life from my backwards Neo-Puritan relatives.<br /> <br /> Seriously, my family was so Puritanical that not only did they ban Halloween for having Pagan roots, they also banned Christmas and Easter for having Pagan roots when I was a kid. So, naturally I do not like Demon: The Fallen or its setting assumptions. It's like a bad crossover fanfiction between Paradise Lost, Menmoch The Devil, and Chick Tracts.<br /> <br /> In my World of Darkness head-canon, Demon: The Fallen does not exist and neither does its cosmology (I also strike down KOTE and Wraith gets treated as a very loose &quot;Broad Strokes&quot; form of canon). While there was definitely a First Vampire, nobody knows if it was really Caine or not. In my games, Noddism and the whole Caine legend came about during the Early Middle Ages as Christianity became more prevalent among Kindred.<br /> <br /> BUT if you like Demon and want it in your games, that's fine with me. More power to you. You do you and I'll do me.<br /> <br /> Just don't tell me I'm playing the game wrong for rejecting Demon and its Abrahamic-inspired cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 04-05-2018, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T10:08:25-07:00","id":1203443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203437#post1203437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've renounced Christianity and I am a Classical Greco-Roman Pagan (I used to be an atheist before that) but I utterly despise Demon: The Fallen for many reasons.<br /> <br /> The chief reasons being the fact that WW proposed Demon's cosmology as the &quot;One True Way&quot; cosmology for the World of Darkness for a while. The fact that it depends on the Revised Edition metaplot (which I also strongly dislike) doesn't help matters either.<br /> <br /> Then there's the material found in the Earthbound book that basically states that the evil Earthbound invented Paganism, which is eerily similar to the whole &quot;Pagan Gods are actually evil Demons&quot; argument that a lot of fundamentalist Christians put forward, and that I have had to put up with in real life from my backwards Neo-Puritan relatives.<br /> <br /> Seriously, my family was so Puritanical that not only did they ban Halloween for having Pagan roots, they also banned Christmas and Easter for having Pagan roots when I was a kid. So, naturally I do not like Demon: The Fallen or its setting assumptions. It's like a bad crossover fanfiction between Paradise Lost, Menmoch The Devil, and Chick Tracts.<br /> <br /> In my World of Darkness head-canon, Demon: The Fallen does not exist and neither does its cosmology (I also strike down KOTE and Wraith gets treated as a very loose &quot;Broad Strokes&quot; form of canon). While there was definitely a First Vampire, nobody knows if it was really Caine or not. In my games, Noddism and the whole Caine legend came about during the Early Middle Ages as Christianity became more prevalent among Kindred.<br /> <br /> BUT if you like Demon and want it in your games, that's fine with me. More power to you. You do you and I'll do me.<br /> <br /> Just don't tell me I'm playing the game wrong for rejecting Demon and its Abrahamic-inspired cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I find myself wanting to compliment them for recognizing that those holidays have nothing to do with Christianity. Not many christians understand that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But if I remember correctly, God doesn't outright state that there are no other deities, he actually commands that no other deities should be placed above him. Jews used to be polytheistic, but eventually transitioned to monotheism, because the worshipers of YHVH (the Hebrew god of war) forced them to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in C20, it states that the Hsien are considered low rank gods by their native cultures and they draw strength from the worship of mortals. It also states they were kicked out of heaven by the higher ranking gods, so clearly there's more at play than just the Abrahamic creator.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> oh shit, that pretty much sounds like Demon without the Torment, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> But I sympathize with you on the personalized cosmology. In my Chronicles of Darkness, I do not acknowledge the existence of the God Machine or anything related to it. God Machine comes across as too much science fiction and not enough supernatural for my liking. So if something in the established lore is explicitly connected with the God Machine, i simply ignore it, or I retcon the lore to something more appealing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2018, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T13:05:48-07:00","id":1203495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203437#post1203437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've renounced Christianity and I am a Classical Greco-Roman Pagan (I used to be an atheist before that) but I utterly despise Demon: The Fallen for many reasons.<br /> <br /> The chief reasons being the fact that WW proposed Demon's cosmology as the &quot;One True Way&quot; cosmology for the World of Darkness for a while. The fact that it depends on the Revised Edition metaplot (which I also strongly dislike) doesn't help matters either.<br /> <br /> Then there's the material found in the Earthbound book that basically states that the evil Earthbound invented Paganism, which is eerily similar to the whole &quot;Pagan Gods are actually evil Demons&quot; argument that a lot of fundamentalist Christians put forward, and that I have had to put up with in real life from my backwards Neo-Puritan relatives.<br /> <br /> Seriously, my family was so Puritanical that not only did they ban Halloween for having Pagan roots, they also banned Christmas and Easter for having Pagan roots when I was a kid. So, naturally I do not like Demon: The Fallen or its setting assumptions. It's like a bad crossover fanfiction between Paradise Lost, Menmoch The Devil, and Chick Tracts.<br /> <br /> In my World of Darkness head-canon, Demon: The Fallen does not exist and neither does its cosmology (I also strike down KOTE and Wraith gets treated as a very loose &quot;Broad Strokes&quot; form of canon). While there was definitely a First Vampire, nobody knows if it was really Caine or not. In my games, Noddism and the whole Caine legend came about during the Early Middle Ages as Christianity became more prevalent among Kindred.<br /> <br /> BUT if you like Demon and want it in your games, that's fine with me. More power to you. You do you and I'll do me.<br /> <br /> Just don't tell me I'm playing the game wrong for rejecting Demon and its Abrahamic-inspired cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I abandoned christianity when I got older as well. Being served a heaping load of nonsense didn't endear me to the abrahamic faiths all that much.<br /> <br /> I read that section as well. I didn't get entirely the same thing out of it, but it was close enough that in hindsight I'm surprised I didn't chuck something out a window.<br /> <br /> Anyway I don't see an issue with rejected it wholesale if you don't find it fun. I made The Creator into a lesser Vanir after all. Would be hypocritical say someone is wrong for doing it. Not to mention my loathing of Changeling.... I loathed it so much that I told my players that fae and sidhe are in a losing war against the actual mythological elves(which are from norse myths and have nothing to do with fae and sidhe). I only acknowledged it because a player wanted to play a fae vampire bloodline and I was too nice to say no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203443#post1203443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I find myself wanting to compliment them for recognizing that those holidays have nothing to do with Christianity. Not many christians understand that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But if I remember correctly, God doesn't outright state that there are no other deities, he actually commands that no other deities should be placed above him. Jews used to be polytheistic, but eventually transitioned to monotheism, because the worshipers of YHVH (the Hebrew god of war) forced them to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in C20, it states that the Hsien are considered low rank gods by their native cultures and they draw strength from the worship of mortals. It also states they were kicked out of heaven by the higher ranking gods, so clearly there's more at play than just the Abrahamic creator.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> oh shit, that pretty much sounds like Demon without the Torment, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> But I sympathize with you on the personalized cosmology. In my Chronicles of Darkness, I do not acknowledge the existence of the God Machine or anything related to it. God Machine comes across as too much science fiction and not enough supernatural for my liking. So if something in the established lore is explicitly connected with the God Machine, i simply ignore it, or I retcon the lore to something more appealing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah thats mildly put. The amount of christians aware of it aren't very many. Which makes certain nonsensical things thats shown up the past years rather chuckleworthy.<br /> <br /> As for the God-Machine, I like the concept and was gonna use it in the oWoD campaign, but a moment where it fits hasn't come up. Granted its more the general idea than straight up as it is in Chronicles. As for the sciency fiction thing, I just chose to interpret the God-Machine as the maintainer of the physical rules of reality and their ultimate expression, but thats just me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T15:36:56-07:00","id":1203545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203495#post1203495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the God-Machine, I like the concept and was gonna use it in the oWoD campaign, but a moment where it fits hasn't come up. Granted its more the general idea than straight up as it is in Chronicles. As for the sciency fiction thing, I just chose to interpret the God-Machine as the maintainer of the physical rules of reality and their ultimate expression, but thats just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my initial take on it, but that gave me the impression that the God Machine chronicle was basically World of Darkness: The Matrix.<br /> <br /> And many people on these very forums got mad at me for that, saying that it was both untrue and unfair to the creators to spread misinformation about the game.<br /> <br /> So now, the only way I can describe the GMC, Demons and Angels is being some form of hyper advanced Artificial Intelligence with access to technology so far beyond our comprehension, that we would interpret it to be the work of the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T16:54:51-07:00","id":1203567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203437#post1203437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just don't tell me I'm playing the game wrong for rejecting Demon and its Abrahamic-inspired cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone was doing that. Or at least, I can say I wasn't. You are totally free to run the game how you wish, and I think your game sounds pretty coo'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:13:55-07:00","id":1203577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203567#post1203567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone was doing that. Or at least, I can say I wasn't. You are totally free to run the game how you wish, and I think your game sounds pretty coo'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't accusing anyone specifically, but I've been told I've been &quot;playing the game wrong&quot; on multiple forums (including this one) for rejecting the metaplot and personal horror in my games.<br /> <br /> So I get defensive at times. I do sincerely apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:35:23-07:00","id":1203636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203545#post1203545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That was my initial take on it, but that gave me the impression that the God Machine chronicle was basically World of Darkness: The Matrix.<br /> <br /> And many people on these very forums got mad at me for that, saying that it was both untrue and unfair to the creators to spread misinformation about the game.<br /> <br /> So now, the only way I can describe the GMC, Demons and Angels is being some form of hyper advanced Artificial Intelligence with access to technology so far beyond our comprehension, that we would interpret it to be the work of the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I don't blame you. Everything I've read about Demon the Descent makes the gameline come across like it was given the wrong name with the wrong terms used since nothing about it feels particularly demonic or angelic. Wouldn't surprise me that it was inspired by the simulation theory either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:59:04-07:00","id":1203648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203636#post1203636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah I don't blame you. Everything I've read about Demon the Descent makes the gameline come across like it was given the wrong name with the wrong terms used since nothing about it feels particularly demonic or angelic. Wouldn't surprise me that it was inspired by the simulation theory either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again...<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t like nor \u2018click\u2019 with Descent\u2019s themes and aesthetics\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cDescent is wrong for not portraying demons, angels and God as anything but what Judeo-Christian lore &amp; apocrypha says.\u201d<br /> <br /> One is bound to invite a certain type of response, especially from people who do like how Descent does it \u2018wrong,\u2019 and people who not only cares not for Christianity but whose cultural background isn\u2019t even indirectly affected by it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And besides, Descent is based on Gnosticism anyway. It all fits if you just replace every mention of \u201cGod-Machine\u201d as \u201cDemiurge.\u201d And there are too many people thinking the Machine is like Autochthon, when it\u2019s more closer to the Weaver.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Forgot to add the spy genre as Descent\u2019s main motifs. Hell, even the high-tech stuff can relate to the spy genre and not science fiction - I mean, look at all the shiny toys, wicked stunts, and mad intrigue &amp; maneuvering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:15:05-07:00","id":1203656,"title":"","content":"My personal opinion is DtD is very much a &quot;fallen&quot; story. They were servants who rebelled. In my head, I picture the pitch meeting going something like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah let's do a Demon line!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure\u2014wait, we can't. People didn't like how the last one was all based on Paradise Lost. Like we were promoting Christianity or something.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So what do we do?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Let's strip away any hint of religion and make it about a God Machine.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Brilliant!&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the mechanics of DtD and I like the story, but it doesn't fit in my World of Darkness as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:20:35-07:00","id":1203659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203656#post1203656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the mechanics of DtD and I like the story, but it doesn't fit in my World of Darkness as is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly. If Descent was created as its own completely separate game line, I wouldn't have had a problem with it. But as part of the Chronicles of Darkness, it really does not mesh well with the rest of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:21:28-07:00","id":1203861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203659#post1203659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Exactly. If Descent was created as its own completely separate game line, I wouldn't have had a problem with it. But as part of the Chronicles of Darkness, it really does not mesh well with the rest of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Prometheans and alchemists get Weird Science, and mages can go full-on magitech if they want to, and a part of Descent's point is that its monsters are this bunch of divinely distant outsiders that even other monsters who go bump in the night have no idea what they're <i>really </i>dealing with...<br /> <br /> Anyways! Speaking less of preferences for DtD and more of virtues of DtF, and with a mention of Promethean, how successful are the Fallen (not the Earthbound NPCs) at playing God in the sense of breaking taboos of &quot;only God can do it&quot; sort of monotheistic blasphemies? (We do know they're not shabby at playing lowercase-g gods, with all the cults running around...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:47:27-07:00","id":1203870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203861#post1203861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, Prometheans and alchemists get Weird Science, and mages can go full-on magitech if they want to, and a part of Descent's point is that its monsters are this bunch of divinely distant outsiders that even other monsters who go bump in the night have no idea what they're <i>really </i>dealing with...<br /> <br /> Anyways! Speaking less of preferences for DtD and more of virtues of DtF, and with a mention of Promethean, how successful are the Fallen (not the Earthbound NPCs) at playing God in the sense of breaking taboos of &quot;only God can do it&quot; sort of monotheistic blasphemies? (We do know they're not shabby at playing lowercase-g gods, with all the cults running around...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also don't care much for Promethean. I'm already human, I don't see the point in playing a game that revolves around trying to become one. Although I do understand the kind of narrative they were going for. As for mage <i>&quot;If they want to&quot;</i> being the key phrase there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The effectiveness of Demons in Fallen seems to be related to which house / caste or whatever they belonged to before the Fall.<br /> <br /> Defilers, for example, can change your physical appearance. But I'm given to understand that it's mostly cosmetic. If you actually want to improve your physical performance, you want to contact a Devourer.<br /> <br /> And that involves flesh crafting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2018, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:56:57-07:00","id":1203958,"title":"","content":"I would think the problem a player would run into with a Fallen attempting play god or God in the modern night is that it would attract all kinds of wrong attention. If it is a DtF only story, plenty of other Fallen might try to interfere because it endangers the rest of them; or, alternatively, get jealous and attempt to usurp this new savior and take his flock. If it is crossgenre, then pretty much every other splat would have factions suddenly going after this would be deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:25:41-07:00","id":1203984,"title":"","content":"So, the usual uphill effort. Well, at least we get to be a legitimate fallen angel/ old god while doing it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T16:26:15-07:00","id":1204027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203984#post1203984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the usual uphill effort. Well, at least we get to be a legitimate fallen angel/ old god while doing it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that you're playing one of the <b>weakest</b> types of demon. The real heavy hitters are either still trapped in the Abyss, or members of the Earthbound. So just because your demon isn't some mighty elder god doesn't mean they don't exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:14:26-07:00","id":1204113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1204027#post1204027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that you're playing one of the <b>weakest</b> types of demon. The real heavy hitters are either still trapped in the Abyss, or members of the Earthbound. So just because your demon isn't some mighty elder god doesn't mean they don't exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And hey, a demon\u2019s got to aspire something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So far it certainly looks like DtF can provide a play experience/meaning that the existing CofD lines don\u2019t quite touch. Even if that makes the world cluttered with \u201cdemons,\u201d that\u2019s a good sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T03:01:08-07:00","id":1204149,"title":"","content":"While DtD is not high on my list of Chronicles of Darkness games I am a big fan of, there are no less than three game lines for Chronicles that many of the themes of DtD meshed extremely well with. Not liking it is one thing but the idea it doesn't mesh with the setting overall is laughable.<br /> <br /> As for Demon the Fallen. It suffered from a lot of problems that first editions tend to have. It's mechanics in areas were poor and need of serious fixing and it had some setting problems(particularly some problematic things in the mostly good Earthbound book) that could all be remedied in say a 20th anniversary book perhaps. But there is enough compelling material left to work with certainly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 04-07-2018, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:45:32-07:00","id":1204176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1204149#post1204149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While DtD is not high on my list of Chronicles of Darkness games I am a big fan of, there are no less than three game lines for Chronicles that many of the themes of DtD meshed extremely well with. Not liking it is one thing but the idea it doesn't mesh with the setting overall is laughable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I mean is that I bought World of Darkness because it revolved around the supernatural being present in our modern day world. And for the most part, the game lines have kept to that theme with vampires, werewolves, mummies, witches, faeries and all that good stuff.<br /> <br /> I did not sign up for a futuristic sci-fi thriller, which Descent appears to be largely influenced by. It does not fit with the rest of the theme World of Darkness had going for it. Which is why I say that it doesn't mesh well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire: I'm a blood drinking corpse with mystical powers.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: I'm a shapeshifting shaman with spiritual powers.<br /> <br /> Changeling: I'm a creature straight out of your dreams, with magical powers.<br /> <br /> Demon: I'm a combination of Neo, GLaDos, and Shodan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-07-2018, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:05:15-07:00","id":1204228,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Let\u2019s take the D:tD talk to the CofD forums, please. It\u2019s beginning to detract from the topic at hand.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:38:16-07:00","id":1204239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1203958#post1203958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think the problem a player would run into with a Fallen attempting play god or God in the modern night is that it would attract all kinds of wrong attention. If it is a DtF only story, plenty of other Fallen might try to interfere because it endangers the rest of them; or, alternatively, get jealous and attempt to usurp this new savior and take his flock. If it is crossgenre, then pretty much every other splat would have factions suddenly going after this would be deity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The things is, though, that demons draw their power from the worship of mortals. And I don't see them inspiring too much faith by maintaining a low profile out of fear of being targeted by others. Mortals, cultists especially, want their patrons to be grandiose and powerful. That's why they pray to them, so that they can achieve things that would not normally be possible under their own power. If word gets out that their demon lord is afraid of another demon and doesn't wan to attract notice, they'll probably defect over to their side. Unless the demon has stripped them of their ability to do so.<br /> <br /> And if I understand correctly, the end times scenario involves Lucifer announcing himself to the world by manifesting his true form over an entire city and leaving it there for several days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T22:47:58-07:00","id":1207550,"title":"","content":"Just spitballing here, but maybe Lucifer isn't as concerned about the risks involved in other supernaturals taking umbrage at him being indiscreet as PC-level characters ought to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T19:07:24-07:00","id":1207837,"title":"","content":"Considering Lucifer never suffered the issues brought on by the Abyss and was never cursed beyond being forced to walk the earth, at least to my knowledge, he likely wouldn't give two figs about what other supernaturals think unless they pose a direct threat to his own plans. Not like he needs to secure worship in the modern day either given the widespread abrahamic religions and there being at least one branch that pretty much worships one version of him. So he's not gonna run out of power anytime soon. Lucifer pretty much occupies a similar position to Caine in terms of power level(ie whatever the GM needs). At least thats my impressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T06:03:43-07:00","id":1207957,"title":"","content":"Lucifer &gt; Arcangels that cursed Caine &gt; Caine. In my opinion<br /> <br /> But he does risk getting killed by the joined effort of the Archdukes, that's why he didn't show his cards for milenia, instead fighting trough proxy (creating demon hunter orders and trying to erase faith in the age of reason. He chooses to risk his life at the end)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Lucifer never suffered the issues brought on by the Abyss and was never cursed beyond being forced to walk the earth, at least to my knowledge, he likely wouldn't give two figs about what other supernaturals think unless they pose a direct threat to his own plans. Not like he needs to secure worship in the modern day either given the widespread abrahamic religions and there being at least one branch that pretty much worships one version of him. So he's not gonna run out of power anytime soon. Lucifer pretty much occupies a similar position to Caine in terms of power level(<b>ie whatever the GM needs</b>). At least thats my impressions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the GM needs doesn't equal invincibility. The GM may choose that Lucifer can't show himself without suffering nasty consequences, as the fabled Antediluvian (also GM fiat power level) soon discovered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T06:26:36-07:00","id":1207959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1207837#post1207837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not like he needs to secure worship in the modern day either given the widespread abrahamic religions and there being at least one branch that pretty much worships one version of him..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Assuming you're referring to modern day Satanists, that's not completely accurate. They don't worship the devil, per se, but rather they seek to emulate him. Satan's name means &quot;the Adversary&quot; and by taking on the role of the adversary themselves, they take on the role of Satan.<br /> <br /> Modern Satanism has more in common with the ideal of worshiping yourself, rather than some outside power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T07:32:14-07:00","id":1207980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1207959#post1207959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming you're referring to modern day Satanists, that's not completely accurate. They don't worship the devil, per se, but rather they seek to emulate him. Satan's name means &quot;the Adversary&quot; and by taking on the role of the adversary themselves, they take on the role of Satan.<br /> <br /> Modern Satanism has more in common with the ideal of worshiping yourself, rather than some outside power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Taking in count the context , probably wasn't talking about them but about the ones that actually worship the devil. It gets confusing because those post-modern Crowley-like &quot;Satanists&quot; you're taking about took that name for the reasons you stated, disregarding the fact that people that worship mythical Satan do exist.<br /> <br /> However, while I'm sure that worshiping no one ain't going to fuel faith to anyone, I'm not so sure that worshiping &quot;the devil&quot; counts as giving faith to Lucifer any more than it would give faith to more devilish devils (like pretty much every demon but Lucifer). After all, Lucifer it's a fake name, and the imaginery doesn't fit either. Heck, Satanists, by worshiping themselves, are more luciferian-friendly than devil worshipers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-17-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T04:53:17-07:00","id":1208396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1207957#post1207957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucifer &gt; Arcangels that cursed Caine &gt; Caine. In my opinion<br /> <br /> But he does risk getting killed by the joined effort of the Archdukes, that's why he didn't show his cards for milenia, instead fighting trough proxy (creating demon hunter orders and trying to erase faith in the age of reason. He chooses to risk his life at the end)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Whatever the GM needs doesn't equal invincibility. The GM may choose that Lucifer can't show himself without suffering nasty consequences, as the fabled Antediluvian (also GM fiat power level) soon discovered</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I know Lucifer isn't invincible. In terms of power, I'd place him far above antediluvians though due to the way angelic abilities work in DtF and the fact that his powers were never stripped from him in any fashion. Plus no abyss slicing his essence up with its antithesis winds like it happened to the others(winds being figurative since different demons experiences the abyss slightly differently from what I can tell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1207959#post1207959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming you're referring to modern day Satanists, that's not completely accurate. They don't worship the devil, per se, but rather they seek to emulate him. Satan's name means &quot;the Adversary&quot; and by taking on the role of the adversary themselves, they take on the role of Satan.<br /> <br /> Modern Satanism has more in common with the ideal of worshiping yourself, rather than some outside power.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wasn't thinking of satanists no for the very reasons you said. I was thinking of a particular religion in the middle east that appearantly places Lucifer on the worship pedestal in some fashion. Though I'm not terribly familiar with the religion myself and reading up on it, it sounds like it might be Lucifer or it might not. The religion in question is called &quot;Yezidi&quot; if you wish to look it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:47:02-07:00","id":1209004,"title":"","content":"If I were to use Lucifer as an NPC in my game, I would strip the static effects of his known evocations and give them Sphere-like dynamic powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T04:24:00-07:00","id":1209171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1209004#post1209004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to use Lucifer as an NPC in my game, I would strip the static effects of his known evocations and give them Sphere-like dynamic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucifer would have five dots in just about any sphere except Spirit, but statting Lucifer kind of misses the point of someone on his power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:24:41-07:00","id":1209235,"title":"","content":"As the saying goes &quot;if it has stats, we can beat it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:36:00-07:00","id":1209269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1209235#post1209235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the saying goes &quot;if it has stats, we can beat it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, yeah, but sometimes the stat block says stuff like 'eats 1d10 characters a round.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:42:14-07:00","id":1209272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1209235#post1209235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the saying goes &quot;if it has stats, we can beat it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are some videos on youtube describing how to do <b>MILLIONS</b> worth of damage in D&amp;D using fucking cantrip spells!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:50:45-07:00","id":1209294,"title":"","content":"My problem with Demon is mostly lore-wise. I think they explain too much about the nature of the rebellion and the origin of demons. &quot;This is exactly what happened, this is why it happened, it's not up for debate&quot; when it would have been more interesting to go with a New World of Darkness style &quot;maybe it went down like this, or maybe like that. Maybe God was evil, maybe he was good. Maybe Lucifer was good, maybe he was evil&quot;. I think that would have left things more open to player interpretation.<br /> <br /> I also think the developers missed a <b><i>golden</i> </b>opportunity by focussing on the fallen-angel element rather than sin like in Inferno. The whole idea of &quot;Seven Deadly Sins&quot; had been practically gift-wrapped for the devs when coming up with demonic houses. Instead they went with the whole idea of basing them off the roles the Fallen had during the creation of Earth, which led to a bunch of weird Lores and Apocalyptic forms which sounded like they belonged more in a superhero comic than any kind of horror story.<br /> <br /> Any look at demonic vestments for the possessed in Inferno and you see a wealth of potential powers for a sin/vice-based splat to make use of which would have been thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> You had the potential for a truly twisted gameline based on human vice and immorality, and how it might interact with things in the WoD. You could also have brought in Angels, scary emissaries of Heavenly Wrath, as secondary antagonists along with the Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Even though I like Fallen a LOT more than Descent I still feel it was a missed opportunity in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T20:30:10-07:00","id":1230451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1198778#post1198778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also has startlingly bad fluff in a demon mentioning that autistic people have weak connections to their souls and make for easily-had vessels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As an autistic person, I can say my connection to my soul is perfectly fine. Thankfully this seems to be going the way of the Wu-Keng.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T22:49:02-07:00","id":1230468,"title":"","content":"Was this something from the Core? I remember things like catatonic/Comatose people being suitable targets as well as those who fried their brains from constant drug use or another form of brain damage, but did they say autistic people in like a chapter fiction or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T14:13:50-07:00","id":1234087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198332-yay-or-nay-demon-the-fallen?p=1230468#post1230468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was this something from the Core? I remember things like catatonic/Comatose people being suitable targets as well as those who fried their brains from constant drug use or another form of brain damage, but did they say autistic people in like a chapter fiction or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 82 of the core book, in a conversation between Ahrimal and his thrall Hannah:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Fallen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cWhat about the mentally ill?\u201d Hannah says.<br /> <br /> I nod. \u201cMental instabilities like severe autism render the host incapable of truly exerting their free will, making them vulnerable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut what about their souls? Are they also\u2026 weakly tethered?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot so much weakly tethered as simply unable to assert their will in opposition to ours. As to what happens to them\u2026 honestly it depends. Some are forced out of their body, to whatever fate awaits them, while others, I suspect, are driven deep into the recesses of their brains, helpless to interfere with the demon\u2019s wishes. So, yes, we possess the insane. We find them in Gropiusstadt alleyways, with so many track-lines that their veins have collapsed and left long clefts up their arm. We find them in the deepest, darkest rooms of Invalidenhaus or in the rest homes for the elderly, which are some times far worse than any asylum. When it comes down to it,\u201d I admit, \u201cwe are demons, most times even after we find a host.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T15:27:18-07:00","id":1234102,"title":"","content":"I think I read that part differently from some people here, I always assumed it just meant they effectively had less ability to say &quot;no&quot; to the invading demon. He even says right there, it doesn't mean their souls are more weakly tethered really. And he does specify &quot;severe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, I love Demon. I love how everything about them is so intensely emotional and they don't really know how to deal with it. I love that Lucifer and all of the Fallen aren't necessarily the villains at all, but they could be. I don't mind that it's loosely inspired by Abrahamic mythology and encompasses all other mythology in a &quot;lesser&quot; way (I'm not really any sort of religious, so I don't have much investment there). I don't mind that it lays out so much of the backstory, it's a good read that helps establish a lot of the foundations and then you're free to mess with present-day dynamics as you like. Time in the Abyss, the host's nature, and fuzzy memories of the war all have major effects on how the fallen remember and interpret those early days, and how they see each other now. At the same time, you are playing beings who have existed continuously since that time, not descendants 15 to 1000 generations removed, so it makes sense that there should be some established common ground and absolute truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T19:34:18-07:00","id":1234138,"title":"","content":"Yeah it specifically is saying they aren\u2019t weakly tethered to their soul, they are just more vulnerable to resisting a demon, and it sounds like it\u2019s specifically talking about severe nonfunctional levels of autism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}